{"id": "185127", "name": "הרכבת פונקציה עם מסילות – התאמת נוסחאות מסילה לגרף ההרכבה (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "functions": [{"name": "f1", "params": ["t"], "body": "f1"}, {"name": "f2", "params": ["t"], "body": "f2"}, {"name": "f3", "params": ["t"], "body": "f3"}], "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Let \\(f(x,y)={{CT:0}}\\) Here is the graph of \\(f(x,y)\\):</p><div style=\"text-align:center\"><img src=\"data/185127/files/1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"258\" height=\"250\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"></div><p>Three functions \\(\\alpha_i:[a,b] \\rightarrow R^2\\) are given by their formulas below. Match each one with the number of the graph of its composition with \\(f(x,y)={{CT:0}}\\).</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;gap:12px\"><div style=\"flex:0 1 360px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">Graph 1:</div>{{CT:1}}</div><div style=\"flex:0 1 360px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">Graph 2:</div>{{CT:2}}</div><div style=\"flex:0 1 360px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">Graph 3:</div>{{CT:3}}</div></div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>(Please answer with 1, 2 or 3)</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(\\alpha_1(t)=({{CT:4}}, {{CT:5}})\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Graph number of \\(f(\\alpha_1(t))\\): [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"></div><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(\\alpha_2(t)=({{CT:6}}, {{CT:7}})\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Graph number of \\(f(\\alpha_2(t))\\): [[input:ans2]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans2]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"></div><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(\\alpha_3(t)=({{CT:8}}, {{CT:9}})\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Graph number of \\(f(\\alpha_3(t))\\): [[input:ans3]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans3]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Substitute each path into \\(f\\): if \\(\\alpha(t)=(x(t),y(t))\\) then \\((f\\circ\\alpha)(t)=f(x(t),y(t))\\). Then compare simple features of the three resulting functions of \\(t\\) (periodic or not, the size of the values, the value at \\(t=0\\)) with the three graphs.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The three compositions</b><br>The three paths that appear in the question give the following compositions with \\(f(x,y)={{CT:0}}\\):<ul><li>\\(\\alpha(t)=(\\cos t,\\sin t)\\): <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(\\cos t,\\sin t)={{CT:10}} \\]</p>a \\(2\\pi\\)-periodic function with \\(|f(\\alpha(t))|\\le 2+1=3\\) and \\(f(\\alpha(0))={{CT:11}}\\). This is <b>Graph 1</b>.</li><li>\\(\\alpha(t)=(3t,t^2)\\): <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(3t,t^2)={{CT:12}} \\]</p>a polynomial of degree 4, not periodic, with \\(f(\\alpha(0))={{CT:13}}\\) and huge values for large \\(|t|\\) (for example \\(f(\\alpha(2\\pi))\\approx {{CT:14}}\\)). This is <b>Graph 2</b>.</li><li>\\(\\alpha(t)=(3\\sin t,\\cos t)\\): <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(3\\sin t,\\cos t)={{CT:15}} \\]</p>again \\(2\\pi\\)-periodic, but now \\(f(\\alpha(0))={{CT:16}}\\), \\(f(\\alpha(\\pi/2))={{CT:17}}\\) and the values reach about \\(\\pm 9.4\\). This is <b>Graph 3</b>.</li></ul></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The matching</b><br>Each of your paths is one of these three:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\(\\alpha_1(t)=({{CT:4}}, {{CT:5}})\\ \\longrightarrow\\ \\text{Graph }{{CT:18}}\\)</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\(\\alpha_2(t)=({{CT:6}}, {{CT:7}})\\ \\longrightarrow\\ \\text{Graph }{{CT:19}}\\)</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\(\\alpha_3(t)=({{CT:8}}, {{CT:9}})\\ \\longrightarrow\\ \\text{Graph }{{CT:20}}\\)</p>Hence<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\alpha_1:\\ {{CT:18}},\\qquad \\alpha_2:\\ {{CT:19}},\\qquad \\alpha_3:\\ {{CT:20}} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]<br />[[feedback:prt2]]<br />[[feedback:prt3]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p>Correct answer, well done.</p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p>Incorrect answer.</p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans3", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "sol1", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The first match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The first match is incorrect, {{CT:21}} is the correct graph.</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans2", "tans": "sol2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The second match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The second match is incorrect, {{CT:22}} is the correct graph.</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt3", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans3", "tans": "sol3", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The third match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The third match is incorrect, {{CT:23}} is the correct graph.</div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["a", "b", "f", "f1", "f11", "f2", "f22", "f3", "f33", "lst_trigo", "path_lst", "sol1", "sol2", "sol3", "x1", "x11", "x2", "x22", "x3", "x33", "y1", "y11", "y2", "y22", "y3", "y33"], "nvariants": 50}